--- This file defines the sessions between a client and a TA: opening a session, and invoking a
--- command in it ([Internal Core] 4.3, 4.5, 4.9, [Client API] 4.5.7, 4.5.9).
---
--- The TrustedOS keeps every open session in sess: sessionId(N) |-> session(CL, TI), the
--- client CL and the TA instance TI that serves it.  The client is an RA, reeClient(RI), or a TA,
--- taClient(TK).  Both kinds of client go through the TrustedOS in the same way, and the
--- TrustedOS answers each through its own channel:
---
---                       RA client (TEEC_*)                  TA client (TEE_*TASession, ...)
---   open request        smcReq(RI, TeecOpenSession, ...)    reqTrustedOS(openTASession(TN), TK)
---   open answer         smcRet(RI, (# success # SID), CS)   retTrustedOS(openSessionSuccess(SID), TK)
---   invoke request      smcReq(RI, TeecInvokeCommand, ...)  msg reqInvoke[...] from TK to KI
---   to the TA instance  msg invkTa[SID, FID, VL, CS] from KI to TI
---   from the instance   msg invkTaRet[SID, CS] from TI to KI
---   invoke answer       smcRet(RI, # success, CS)           msg finishReqInvoke[...] from KI to TK
---
--- An RA holds the session as the value # SID; a TA holds a handle, a TaSessionHandle object
--- whose session attribute is SID.  The TA instance records the session of the request it serves
--- in its client-service, {SID, FID}, so that the TrustedOS finds the client of its answer.
---
--- Opening a session.  The TrustedOS decides in the same way for both kinds of client:
---   * the TA TN has no instance: the TrustedOS creates the instance from the program of TN in
---     ta-prog-map, with its storage, records it in ta-instances, and opens the session on it;
---   * the instance of TN already has a session, and TN accepts one session at a time,
---     taConfig(true, false): TEE_ERROR_BUSY, TEEC_ERROR_BUSY for an RA;
---   * TN has an instance and accepts several sessions, taConfig(true, true): the session is
---     opened on that instance, which all the sessions of TN share, see [Internal Core] 2.1.6;
---   * no TA has the identifier TN: TEE_ERROR_ITEM_NOT_FOUND.
--- Only the single-instance TAs, taConfig(true, MS) in ta-config, are served for now.  The
--- entry points TA_CreateEntryPoint and
--- TA_OpenSessionEntryPoint are not modeled: the instance is created and the session opened at
--- once.  An RA gets the return code, and the new session after success; it is not given the
--- return origin.  A TA gets the code, the handle (TEE_HANDLE_NULL on failure) and the origin.
---
--- Invoking a command.  The TrustedOS forwards the request of the client of a session to the TA
--- instance of the session; a request through a session of another client is not served.  The
--- instance serves one request at a time, see [Internal Core] 2.1.3: the other requests to it
--- wait, as invkTa messages, until it is free, and the next one is chosen nondeterministically.
--- A finished service succeeds, as a service is a void function: the client gets success, with
--- the origin of the TA for a TA client.  A TA instance that panics while it serves the request
--- answers TEE_ERROR_TARGET_DEAD, with the origin of the TEE for a TA client, see [Internal Core]
--- 4.9.3.  In both cases the client gets the memory back as the TA instance has left it.  Every
--- later or waiting request to a panicked instance gets TEE_ERROR_TARGET_DEAD too, with the
--- memory of the client unchanged, see [Internal Core] 2.3.3.
---
--- TEEC_CloseSession and TEE_CloseTASession are not modeled: a session, once open, stays open.
--- The IMP call of an RA, teecOpenSession, is in RICH-APP-BEHAVIOR, and teecInvokeCommand in
--- SHARED-MEMORY-BEHAVIOR.

--- @kind behavior
--- @feature ta-session
omod SESSION-BEHAVIOR is
  pr TEE-OS-BEHAVIOR .
  pr TRUST-APP .
  pr SECURE-MONITOR-CALL .
  pr INVOKE-TA-CALL .
  pr HANDLE-AUX .
  pr TEE-MSG .
  pr TEE-CLIENT-FUNC .
  pr TEE-INTERNAL-CLIENT-FUNC .
  pr TEE-CLIENT-IMP-VALUE .
  pr RETURN-IMP-VALUE .

  op #_ : FuncId -> Value [ctor] .
  op #_ : ArgList -> Value [ctor] .

  op reqInvoke : -> ReqId [ctor] .
  op finishReqInvoke : -> ReqId [ctor] .

  vars KI RI TK TI HANDLE : Oid .
  var CL : Client .
  vars TN TA : AppId .
  var N : Nat .
  var MS : Bool .
  var P : Program .
  vars CS : CStore .
  var SIL : List{Service} .
  var SOL : List{ServiceReturn} .
  vars SID SID' : SessionId .
  var SESS : Map{SessionId,SessionInfo} .
  var PROGC : Map{AppId,ProgramCell} .
  var CFG : Map{AppId,TaConfig} .
  var IM : Map{AppId,Oid} .
  var FID : FuncId .
  var VL : ArgList .
  var PARAMS : ArgList .
  var RET : ReturnCode .
  var RO : ReturnOrigin .
  vars MEM MEM' : Map{Nat,Value?} .
  vars L L' : Nat .
  vars AL AL' : Map{Nat,Nat} .
  var KS : KConfig .
  var ZsTeeOpenTASession1 : Value .
  var ZrTeeOpenTASession : ArgList .
  vars ZsTeeInvokeTACommand1 ZsTeeInvokeTACommand2 : Value .
  var ZrTeeInvokeTACommand : ArgList .

------------------------------------------------------------
--- Opening a session: the TrustedOS, for an RA (TEEC_OpenSession)
------------------------------------------------------------

--- teec-open-session: TN has no instance, so the TrustedOS creates the TA instance oid(N, KI)
--- with the program P of TN and its storage, records it as the instance of TN, and opens the
--- session sessionId(N) of the RA RI on it.  The memory CS of the RA comes back unchanged.
  crl [teec-open-session] :
    smcReq(RI, TeecOpenSession, # TN, CS)
    < KI : TrustedOS | ta-prog-map : (TN |-> [P] , PROGC) ,
                       ta-config : (TN |-> taConfig(true, MS) , CFG) , ta-instances : IM ,
                       sess : SESS , session-counter : N >
    =>
    < KI : TrustedOS | ta-instances : (TN |-> oid(N, KI) , IM) ,
                       sess : (sessionId(N) |-> session(reeClient(RI), oid(N, KI)) , SESS) ,
                       session-counter : N + 1 >
    < oid(N, KI) : TrustedApp | proc : none , prog : P ,
                                 status : (normal).AppStatus , api-call : noCall , counter : 1 ,
                                 storage : oid(0, oid(N, KI)) , os-kernel : KI ,
                                 client-service : none >
    < oid(0, oid(N, KI)) : Storage | status : (normal).StorageStatus , files : empty , counter : 0 >
    smcRet(RI, (# success # sessionId(N)), CS)
  if not $hasMapping(IM, TN) .

--- teec-open-session-busy: the instance TI of TN already has the session SID', and TN accepts
--- one session at a time: TEEC_ERROR_BUSY.
  rl [teec-open-session-busy] :
    smcReq(RI, TeecOpenSession, # TN, CS)
    < KI : TrustedOS | ta-config : (TN |-> taConfig(true, false) , CFG) ,
                       ta-instances : (TN |-> TI , IM) , sess : (SID' |-> session(CL, TI) , SESS) >
    =>
    < KI : TrustedOS | >
    smcRet(RI, # errorBusy, CS) .

--- teec-open-session-shared: TN has the instance TI and accepts several sessions, so the
--- session sessionId(N) of the RA RI is opened on TI.
  rl [teec-open-session-shared] :
    smcReq(RI, TeecOpenSession, # TN, CS)
    < KI : TrustedOS | ta-config : (TN |-> taConfig(true, true) , CFG) ,
                       ta-instances : (TN |-> TI , IM) , sess : SESS , session-counter : N >
    =>
    < KI : TrustedOS | sess : (sessionId(N) |-> session(reeClient(RI), TI) , SESS) ,
                       session-counter : N + 1 >
    smcRet(RI, (# success # sessionId(N)), CS) .

--- teec-open-session-not-found: no TA has the identifier TN: TEEC_ERROR_ITEM_NOT_FOUND.
  crl [teec-open-session-not-found] :
    smcReq(RI, TeecOpenSession, # TN, CS)
    < KI : TrustedOS | ta-prog-map : PROGC >
    =>
    < KI : TrustedOS | >
    smcRet(RI, # errorItemNotFound, CS)
  if not $hasMapping(PROGC, TN) .

------------------------------------------------------------
--- Opening a session: the TrustedOS, for a TA (openTASession)
------------------------------------------------------------

--- open-ta-session: TN has no instance, so the TrustedOS creates the TA instance oid(N, KI) with
--- the program P of TN from ta-prog-map and its storage oid(0, oid(N, KI)) with no files,
--- records it as the instance of TN, and opens the session sessionId(N) of the requesting TA TK
--- on it.  openSessionSuccess(sessionId(N)) is queued in service-out.
  crl [open-ta-session] :
    < KI : TrustedOS | service-in : (openTASession(TN) SIL) , service-out : SOL ,
                       service-request-ta-inst : TK ,
                       ta-prog-map : (TN |-> [P] , PROGC) ,
                       ta-config : (TN |-> taConfig(true, MS) , CFG) , ta-instances : IM ,
                       sess : SESS , session-counter : N >
    =>
    < KI : TrustedOS | service-in : SIL , service-out : (SOL openSessionSuccess(sessionId(N))) ,
                       ta-instances : (TN |-> oid(N, KI) , IM) ,
                       sess : (sessionId(N) |-> session(taClient(TK), oid(N, KI)) , SESS) ,
                       session-counter : N + 1 >
    < oid(N, KI) : TrustedApp | proc : none , prog : P ,
                                 status : (normal).AppStatus , api-call : noCall , counter : 1 ,
                                 storage : oid(0, oid(N, KI)) , os-kernel : KI ,
                                 client-service : none >
    < oid(0, oid(N, KI)) : Storage | status : (normal).StorageStatus , files : empty , counter : 0 >
  if not $hasMapping(IM, TN) .

--- open-ta-session-busy: the instance TI of TN already has the session SID', and TN accepts one
--- session at a time, so the session is not opened: TEE_ERROR_BUSY, [Internal Core] 4.9.1.
  rl [open-ta-session-busy] :
    < KI : TrustedOS | service-in : (openTASession(TN) SIL) , service-out : SOL ,
                       ta-config : (TN |-> taConfig(true, false) , CFG) ,
                       ta-instances : (TN |-> TI , IM) , sess : (SID' |-> session(CL, TI) , SESS) >
    =>
    < KI : TrustedOS | service-in : SIL , service-out : (SOL openSessionFail(errorBusy)) >
  .

--- open-ta-session-shared: TN has the instance TI and accepts several sessions, so the session
--- sessionId(N) of the requesting TA TK is opened on TI.
  rl [open-ta-session-shared] :
    < KI : TrustedOS | service-in : (openTASession(TN) SIL) , service-out : SOL ,
                       service-request-ta-inst : TK ,
                       ta-config : (TN |-> taConfig(true, true) , CFG) ,
                       ta-instances : (TN |-> TI , IM) , sess : SESS , session-counter : N >
    =>
    < KI : TrustedOS | service-in : SIL , service-out : (SOL openSessionSuccess(sessionId(N))) ,
                       sess : (sessionId(N) |-> session(taClient(TK), TI) , SESS) ,
                       session-counter : N + 1 >
  .

--- open-ta-session-not-found: no TA has the identifier TN, so the session is not opened:
--- TEE_ERROR_ITEM_NOT_FOUND, [Internal Core] 4.9.1.
  crl [open-ta-session-not-found] :
    < KI : TrustedOS | service-in : (openTASession(TN) SIL) , service-out : SOL ,
                       ta-prog-map : PROGC >
    =>
    < KI : TrustedOS | service-in : SIL , service-out : (SOL openSessionFail(errorItemNotFound)) >
  if not $hasMapping(PROGC, TN) .

------------------------------------------------------------
--- Opening a session: the TA (TEE_OpenTASession)
------------------------------------------------------------

  --- The 'TEE_OpenTASession' function opens a new session with a Trusted Application.
  --- See page 98 of the G.P. documentation for more details.

  --- open-session-subroutine: the init call of TeeOpenTASession becomes final, and the
  --- TrustedOS is asked to open a session with the TA TA.
  rl [open-session-subroutine] :
    < TK : TAKernel | status : (normal).AppStatus , api-call : init(TeeOpenTASession[# TA ZsTeeOpenTASession1 ZrTeeOpenTASession]) >
    =>
    < TK : TAKernel | api-call : final(TeeOpenTASession[# TA ZsTeeOpenTASession1 ZrTeeOpenTASession]) >
    reqTrustedOS(openTASession(TA) , TK)
  .

  --- open-session-success: the openSessionSuccess(SID) answer of the TrustedOS finishes the
  --- call with success and the handle oid(N, TK) of the session SID, which is created, and the
  --- counter advances by one.
  rl [open-session-success] :
    retTrustedOS(openSessionSuccess(SID), TK)
    < TK : TAKernel | status : (normal).AppStatus , api-call : final(TeeOpenTASession[PARAMS]) , counter : N >
    =>
    < TK : TAKernel | api-call : return(TeeOpenTASession[# success # oid(N, TK) # originTrustedApp]) ,
                      counter : N + 1 >
    freshSessionHandle(N, TK, SID)
  .

  --- open-session-fail: the openSessionFail(RET) answer of the TrustedOS finishes the call with
  --- the code RET, the origin of the TEE, and TEE_HANDLE_NULL as the handle, see [Internal Core]
  --- 4.9.1.  No handle is created.
  rl [open-session-fail] :
    retTrustedOS(openSessionFail(RET), TK)
    < TK : TAKernel | status : (normal).AppStatus , api-call : final(TeeOpenTASession[PARAMS]) >
    =>
    < TK : TAKernel | api-call : return(TeeOpenTASession[# RET # null # originTee]) >
  .

------------------------------------------------------------
--- Invoking a command: the TrustedOS
------------------------------------------------------------

--- handle-smc-request: the TrustedOS forwards the TEEC_InvokeCommand request of the RA RI in its
--- session SID to the TA instance of the session, with the memory CS of the RA.
  rl [handle-smc-request] :
    smcReq(RI, TeecInvokeCommand, (# SID # FID VL), CS)
    < KI : TrustedOS | sess : (SID |-> session(reeClient(RI), TI) , SESS) >
    =>
    < KI : TrustedOS | >
    (msg invkTa[SID, FID, VL, CS] from KI to TI) .

--- handle-session-request: the TrustedOS forwards the TEE_InvokeTACommand request of the TA TK in
--- its session SID to the TA instance of the session, with the memory CS of TK.
  rl [handle-session-request] :
    (msg reqInvoke[# SID # FID # CS # VL] from TK to KI)
    < KI : TrustedOS | sess : (SID |-> session(taClient(TK), TI) , SESS) >
    =>
    < KI : TrustedOS | >
    (msg invkTa[SID, FID, VL, CS] from KI to TI) .

--- handle-smc-request-finish: the TA instance has finished the request of the session SID of the
--- RA RI; the TrustedOS returns the memory as an SMC response with the return code success.
  rl [handle-smc-request-finish] :
    (msg invkTaRet[SID, CS] from TI to KI)
    < KI : TrustedOS | sess : (SID |-> session(reeClient(RI), TI) , SESS) >
    =>
    < KI : TrustedOS | >
    smcRet(RI, # success, CS) .

--- handle-session-request-finish: the TA instance has finished the request of the session SID of
--- the TA TK; the TrustedOS returns the memory to TK with the origin of the TA and success.
  rl [handle-session-request-finish] :
    (msg invkTaRet[SID, CS] from TI to KI)
    < KI : TrustedOS | sess : (SID |-> session(taClient(TK), TI) , SESS) >
    =>
    < KI : TrustedOS | >
    (msg finishReqInvoke[# CS # originTrustedApp # success] from KI to TK) .

--- return-smc-request-panic: a TA instance that panics while it serves the request of the
--- session SID of the RA RI returns target-dead to RI, with the memory as the TA has left it:
--- what the TA wrote before the panic stays.  The TA has no client-service afterwards.
  rl [return-smc-request-panic] :
    < TI : TrustedApp | status : panic, client-service : {SID , FID},
                        proc : (store(MEM) nextLoc(L) arrlen(AL) KS) >
    < KI : TrustedOS | sess : (SID |-> session(reeClient(RI), TI) , SESS) >
    =>
    < KI : TrustedOS | >
    < TI : TrustedApp | status : panic, client-service : none >
    smcRet(RI, # errorTargetDead, cstore(MEM, L, AL)) .

--- return-session-request-panic: a TA instance that panics while it serves the request of the
--- session SID of the TA TK returns TEE_ERROR_TARGET_DEAD with the origin of the TEE to TK, see
--- [Internal Core] 4.9.3, with the memory as the TA has left it.  The TA has no client-service
--- afterwards.
  rl [return-session-request-panic] :
    < TI : TrustedApp | status : panic, client-service : {SID , FID},
                        proc : (store(MEM) nextLoc(L) arrlen(AL) KS) >
    < KI : TrustedOS | sess : (SID |-> session(taClient(TK), TI) , SESS) >
    =>
    < KI : TrustedOS | >
    < TI : TrustedApp | status : panic, client-service : none >
    (msg finishReqInvoke[# cstore(MEM, L, AL) # originTee # errorTargetDead] from KI to TK) .

--- return-smc-request-dead: a request of the session SID of the RA RI to a TA instance that has
--- panicked, waiting or sent after the panic, is not served: TEE_ERROR_TARGET_DEAD, with the
--- memory CS of the RA unchanged.
  rl [return-smc-request-dead] :
    (msg invkTa[SID, FID, VL, CS] from KI to TI)
    < TI : TrustedApp | status : panic >
    < KI : TrustedOS | sess : (SID |-> session(reeClient(RI), TI) , SESS) >
    =>
    < TI : TrustedApp | >
    < KI : TrustedOS | >
    smcRet(RI, # errorTargetDead, CS) .

--- return-session-request-dead: the same for a request of the session SID of the TA TK: the
--- origin is the TEE.
  rl [return-session-request-dead] :
    (msg invkTa[SID, FID, VL, CS] from KI to TI)
    < TI : TrustedApp | status : panic >
    < KI : TrustedOS | sess : (SID |-> session(taClient(TK), TI) , SESS) >
    =>
    < TI : TrustedApp | >
    < KI : TrustedOS | >
    (msg finishReqInvoke[# CS # originTee # errorTargetDead] from KI to TK) .

------------------------------------------------------------
--- Invoking a command: the TA (TEE_InvokeTACommand)
------------------------------------------------------------

  --- The 'TEE_InvokeTACommand' function invokes a command within a session opened between the
  --- client Trusted Application instance and a destination Trusted Application instance.
  --- See page 101 of the G.P. documentation for more details.

  --- invoke-ta-command-subroutine (request): the init call of TeeInvokeTACommand becomes final,
  --- and the reqInvoke message with the session SID of the handle HANDLE, FID, the memory of TK
  --- and VL is sent to the TrustedOS KI of TK.  TK waits for the answer, so its memory does not
  --- change meanwhile.
  rl [invoke-ta-command-subroutine] :
    < TK : TrustedApp | status : (normal).AppStatus , os-kernel : KI ,
                        api-call : init(TeeInvokeTACommand[# HANDLE # FID # VL ZrTeeInvokeTACommand]) ,
                        proc : (store(MEM) nextLoc(L) arrlen(AL) KS) >
    < HANDLE : TaSessionHandle | session : SID >
    =>
    < TK : TrustedApp | api-call : final(TeeInvokeTACommand[# HANDLE # FID # VL ZrTeeInvokeTACommand]) >
    < HANDLE : TaSessionHandle | >
    (msg reqInvoke[# SID # FID # cstore(MEM, L, AL) # VL] from TK to KI)
  .

  --- invoke-ta-command-subroutine (finish): the finishReqInvoke message gives TK its memory
  --- back, as the destination TA has left it, and the return origin RO and the return code RET
  --- to the final call of TeeInvokeTACommand, which becomes return.
  rl [invoke-ta-command-subroutine] :
    (msg finishReqInvoke[# cstore(MEM', L', AL') # RO # RET] from KI to TK)
    < TK : TrustedApp | status : (normal).AppStatus , os-kernel : KI ,
                        api-call : final(TeeInvokeTACommand[# HANDLE ZsTeeInvokeTACommand1 ZsTeeInvokeTACommand2 ZrTeeInvokeTACommand]) ,
                        proc : (store(MEM) nextLoc(L) arrlen(AL) KS) >
    =>
    < TK : TrustedApp | api-call : return(TeeInvokeTACommand[# RET # RO]) ,
                        proc : (store(MEM') nextLoc(L') arrlen(AL') KS) >
  .
endom
